<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation Study on Sampling Strategy: </span>
To validate the impact of the sampling strategy on performance, we adjusted the number of clips <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{\text{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>c</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{\text{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of frames per clip <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thoroughly evaluated the model performance under the same resolution (<math id="S4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224\times 224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224\times 224</annotation></semantics></math>). The experimental results are shown in Table <a href="#S4.T7" title="TABLE VII ‣ IV-E Ablation Study ‣ IV Experiments ‣ EDVD-LLaMA: Explainable Deepfake Video Detection viaMultimodal Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII</span></a>. When the sampling strategy was set to <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\times 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times 9</annotation></semantics></math>, the model achieved the best performance across all metrics. In contrast, reducing <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{\text{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>c</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{\text{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> resulted in performance degradation, especially when the sampling was set to <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>, where the performance dropped significantly. This clearly indicates that fewer clips and frames limit the model’s ability to capture holistic forgery cues in videos, thereby reducing the effectiveness of detection.</p>
</div>
